\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.4}{\ignorespaces Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing this layout, to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered. Using equation (\ref  {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}), the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree } after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in Table \ref  {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.11}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterastigmatism}{{1.4}{12}{Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing this layout, to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered. Using equation (\ref {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}), the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree } after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in Table \ref {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }{figure.caption.11}{}}
